Verse 1:
[D]O [G]where are the reapers that gar[C]ner [G]in
The [D]sheaves of the good from the [G]fields [C]of [G]sin?
With sickles of truth must the [C]work be done,
And [G]no one may rest [C]till the “[G]har[D7]vest [G]home.”
[D]Where are the reapers? O [G]who [D]will [G]come
And [D7]share in the glory [G]of the “[D]harvest home”?
O [G]who will help us to [C]garner in
The [G]sheaves of good [C]from the [G]fields [D7]of [G]sin?

Refrain:
[D]Where are [G]the reapers? [C]O who [G]will come
[D]And share [G]in the [C]glory of [G]the "harvest home"?
[C]O who will help us to garner in
[G]The [C]sheaves of [G]good from [D7]the fields [G]of sin?

Verse 2:
[D]The fields [G]all are [C]ripening, and [G]far and wide
[D]The world [G]now is [C]waiting the [G]harvest tide:
[C]But reapers are few, and the work is great,
[G]And [C]much will [G]be lost [D7]should the [G]harvest wait.

Verse 3:
[D]So come [G]with your [C]sickles, ye [G]sons of men,
[D]And [G]gather together [C]the [G]golden grain;
[C]Toil on till the Lord of the harvest come,
[G]Then [C]share ye [G]His joy [D7]in the [G]"harvest home."
